  "statement": "You're given a list `prices` where `prices[i]` is the price of one share of a stock on day `i`. You may make a single trade: buy on one day, then sell on a later day. Return the largest profit that trade can earn.\n\nIf every possible trade would lose money (or there is only one day), the best move is not to trade at all, so return 0.\n\nConstraints: 1 <= len(prices) <= 10^5; 0 <= prices[i] <= 10^4.",
  "functionName": "max_profit",
  "signature": "def max_profit(prices: list[int]) -> int:",
  "starterCode": "def max_profit(prices: list[int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Return the biggest profit from buying on one day and selling on a later day, or 0 if no trade makes money.\"\"\"\n    pass\n",
  "starterCodeJs": "/**\n * Return the biggest profit from buying on one day and selling on a later day, or 0 if no trade makes money.\n * @param {number[]} prices\n * @return {number}\n */\nfunction maxProfit(prices) {\n\n}\n",
  "examples": [
